C89 Coding Rules

This project strictly follows C89 (ANSI C). All code must compile with a C89-compliant compiler.

All variables MUST be declared at the beginning of a block (function, {}).

Mixing declarations and executable code is FORBIDDEN.

Variables may only be declared after { and before any statements.

Loop variables must be declared outside of for statements.

Function prototypes must be declared before use (typically in header files).

Block scope applies: variables declared inside {} are visible only within that block.

Use K&R braces and 4-space indentation.

Avoid C99+ features entirely.

void example() {
    int i;
    int value;

    for (i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
        int temp;
        value += temp;
    }
}